  it has a consequence beyond the line: a stolen or abandoned session token stays valid for 8 hours instead of 30 — a
  16× wider window for session hijacking on shared or unattended machines, and 16× longer before a revoked/compromised
  account is actually logged out. [38;5;153mserver.js:2[39m confirms this value is the sole expiry control here; there's no
  idle-timeout or re-auth step to limit the blast radius.

  That may well be exactly what you want (long-running internal tool, dev convenience). I just want your explicit
  go-ahead before changing it.
